From c4d03074bc58a8c68bb7173f2efa3019cecb0db9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Alex <05jeelo30@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 23:35:32 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/4] base: Add GameSpace support

Framework side for IRedDragonICY's GameSpace (com.ireddragonicy.gamespace).

Detection and dispatch come from the crDroid 17.0 GameSpace support:
- 5c0bee650d4 core: adding support for game space (rmp22, from AxionOS)
- 2133c5519ab services: Treat gamespace apps as games (rmp22)
- cd8470b5b68 services: Add toggle for gamespace auto detect apps
  (Pranav Vashi)

GameSpaceService tracks the focused app on the default display and
tells GameSpace when a game from gamespace_game_list comes to the
front, and when it leaves or the keyguard shows. While a game is
active, full screen intents are suppressed in SystemUI.

IRedDragonICY's GameSpace expects a game_space binder service, whose
framework patches aren't published, so it is written here:
- IGameSpaceService: registerCallback, unregisterCallback and
  dumpSocketStats (the /proc/net sockets the ping monitor reads), all
  behind MANAGE_GAME_MODE
- IGameSpaceCallback: onGameStart(packageName) and onGameLeave()
Until the app registers its callback, GameStateDispatcher starts its
GameSpaceService with game_start/game_stop instead.

Adapted to AOSPA: the hooks sit next to AOSPA's own code (no
AxSandboxService here), and the bypass-charge path is dropped since it
needs the LineageOS SDK HealthInterface, which AOSPA doesn't ship.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01QY97AsgNLyAwQpzrsxC9zt
